1
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:33,500
. . . One for All and All for Fun!

2
00:08:55,000 --> 00:09:01,000
The Three Musketeers is a action, adventure,
romance film directed by Richard Lester.

3
00:13:22,500 --> 00:13:28,500
In 17th century France, young D'Artagnan wants to join the King's Musketeers, but instead befriends three legendary musketeers—Athos, Porthos, and Aramis—and
together, they become embroiled in the political intrigue surrounding King Louis XIII and his adversaries, particularly the powerful Cardinal Richelieu.

4
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:56,000
D'Artagnan, played by Michael York.

5
00:22:17,500 --> 00:22:23,500
Athos, played by Oliver Reed.

6
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:51,000
Aramis, played by Richard Chamberlain.

7
00:31:12,500 --> 00:31:18,500
Porthos / O'Reilly, played by Frank Finlay.

8
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:46,000
Lady de Winter, played by Faye Dunaway.

9
00:40:07,500 --> 00:40:13,500
Constance de Bonancieux, played by Raquel Welch.

10
00:44:35,000 --> 00:44:41,000
The Three Musketeers (also known as The Three Musketeers (The Queen's Diamonds)) is a
1973 swashbuckler film based on the 1844 novel by Alexandre Dumas.

11
00:49:02,500 --> 00:49:08,500
It is directed by Richard Lester from a screenplay by George
MacDonald Fraser, and produced by Ilya Salkind.

12
00:53:30,000 --> 00:53:36,000
It stars Michael York, Oliver Reed, Frank Finlay, and Richard Chamberlain as the musketeers, with Raquel Welch, Geraldine Chaplin,
Jean-Pierre Cassel, Charlton Heston, Faye Dunaway, Christopher Lee, Simon Ward, Georges Wilson and Spike Milligan.

13
00:57:57,500 --> 00:58:03,500
The film adheres closely to the novel, and also injects a fair amount of humor.

14
01:02:25,000 --> 01:02:31,000
It was proposed in the 1960s as a vehicle for The Beatles, whom
Lester had directed in A Hard Day's Night and Help!

15
01:06:52,500 --> 01:06:58,500
It was shot by David Watkin, with an eye for period
detail, in Madrid and Segovia, Spain.

16
01:11:20,000 --> 01:11:26,000
The fight scenes were choreographed by master swordsman William Hobbs.

17
01:15:47,500 --> 01:15:53,500
The musical score was composed by Michel Legrand.

18
01:20:15,000 --> 01:20:21,000
The Three Musketeers premiered in France on 11 December 1973.

19
01:24:42,500 --> 01:24:48,500
It was both a critical and commercial success and was
nominated for several awards, including five BAFTAs.

20
01:29:10,000 --> 01:29:16,000
Raquel Welch won a Golden Globe for her performance.

21
01:33:37,500 --> 01:33:43,500
The Four Musketeers, a sequel shot back-to-back with its
predecessor, was released the following year.

22
01:38:05,000 --> 01:38:11,000
The film explores themes of france, paris, france,
based on novel or book, swordplay, fight.

23
01:42:32,500 --> 01:42:38,500
The tone is emotional.
